 of these is on this disk under SRC/<tree>/.--------------------------------------------------------------program        SRC/        origin--------------------------------------------------------------REBUILT 2026-08-31, ELEVEN OF THEM.  `cvtbase', `cdiff', `nroff',`etags', `yacc', `xrf', `unstr', `cookhash', `logisim', `pagekwic' and`pagefraz' no longer ship as the binaries their archives carried.  Eachwas broken by the cio selector mismatch -- it linked a `cio.l' whoseputc/getc macros call a trap-13 selector every `cio' module hereimplements as a memory routine, so the program never read its input --and each was rebuilt trap-free from the source in SRC and the recipe intools/rebuild/recipes.psv:  `cc <src> -qm=16k -DOSK -n=<name>'.  Theorigins below are still where the SOURCE came from, which is what thisfile records.  DOC/README-CIO has the measurement.  accordian      accordian   Usenet           comp.sources.games v15i027 (accordian) -- Eric Lechner 1992, public domain  advcom         advint      Usenet           advint.ar  advent         adv         Usenet           adv.ar  advint         advint      Usenet           advint.ar  animal         animal      Usenet           animal.ar  ape            hc_loose    hc disk  SOURCES/USENET/ (loose C sources)  areacode       hc_utils    hc disk  SOURCES/UTILS/  (loose C sources)   [also built from misc]  as0            xasm        microware       MISC/xasm.ar  as1            xasm        microware       MISC/xasm.ar  as4            xasm        microware       MISC/xasm.ar  as5            xasm        microware       MISC/xasm.ar  as11           xasm        microware       MISC/xasm.ar  ascii          misc        Usenet           misc.ar  assembler      eff_gshell  Usenet           eff_gshell.ar  banner         misc        Usenet           misc.ar  bite           v_misc      hc disk  SOURCES/USENET/v_misc.ar  blackjak       effo_snobol EFFO forum disk 9   PROGRAMME/C/SNOBOL  bmgtest     